@startuml replace-inheritance-with-delegation
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam RoundCorner 8
skinparam ClassBorderThickness 2

title Replace Inheritance with Delegation -- Before vs After

package "BEFORE" as before #FFF3F3 {
    skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<before>> #FDEDEC
    skinparam ClassBorderColor<<before>> #E74C3C
    skinparam ClassHeaderBackgroundColor<<before>> #E74C3C

    class "Vector<E>" as VecBefore <<before>> {
        + addElement(item : E) : void
        + removeElementAt(index : int) : void
        + elementAt(index : int) : E
        + insertElementAt(item : E, index : int) : void
        + size() : int
        + isEmpty() : boolean
    }

    class "MyStack<E>" as StackBefore <<before>> {
        + push(item : E) : E
        + pop() : E
        + peek() : E
        ....
        <color:#E74C3C>// PROBLEM: inherits ALL of</color>
        <color:#E74C3C>// Vector's public methods!</color>
        <color:#E74C3C>// Clients can call:</color>
        <color:#E74C3C>// stack.insertElementAt(..)</color>
        <color:#E74C3C>// stack.removeElementAt(..)</color>
        <color:#E74C3C>// Breaks stack semantics!</color>
    }

    VecBefore <|-- StackBefore : <color:#E74C3C>extends</color>
}

note bottom of before
  <color:#E74C3C><b>Problem:</b></color>
  Stack IS-NOT-A Vector.
  Inheritance exposes Vector methods
  that violate LIFO semantics.
  Liskov Substitution violated.
end note

package "AFTER" as after #F0FFF0 {
    skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<after>> #EAFAF1
    skinparam ClassBorderColor<<after>> #27AE60
    skinparam ClassHeaderBackgroundColor<<after>> #27AE60

    class "Vector<E>" as VecAfter <<after>> {
        + addElement(item : E) : void
        + removeElementAt(index : int) : void
        + elementAt(index : int) : E
        + size() : int
        + isEmpty() : boolean
    }

    class "MyStack<E>" as StackAfter <<after>> {
        - <color:#27AE60>vector : Vector<E></color>
        __
        + push(item : E) : E
        + pop() : E
        + peek() : E
        + size() : int
        + isEmpty() : boolean
        ....
        <color:#27AE60>// Only stack operations</color>
        <color:#27AE60>// are exposed.</color>
        <color:#27AE60>// Delegates internally</color>
        <color:#27AE60>// to vector field.</color>
    }

    StackAfter o--> VecAfter : <color:#27AE60>delegates to</color>
}

note bottom of after
  <color:#27AE60><b>Solution:</b></color>
  Stack HAS-A Vector (composition).
  Only push/pop/peek/size/isEmpty
  are exposed. Internal Vector
  is an implementation detail.
  Encapsulation preserved.
end note

before -[hidden]right-> after

@enduml
